The '''player-owned port''' is a high-level [[members]]-only [[minigames|minigame]] that was released on [[11 December]] [[2012]] and expanded on [[7 January]] [[2014]] and again on [[26 January]] [[2015]]. This minigame involves players building their own port to manage a fleet of ships staffed by recruited [[Player-owned port/Captains and crew|crew members]]. These ships explore the [[Wushanko Isles]] on the player's behalf and return with exotic items and supplies that are otherwise unavailable.

Players can start the minigame by entering one of three [[Portal (Player-owned port)|portals]] or the [[ports table]]. The portals are located south-west of [[the Rusty Anchor]] pub in [[Port Sarim]], north-east of [[Prifddinas lodestone]], or in the southern part of the [[Menaphos Port district]]. The ports table is located in [[Fort Forinthry]] in the [[Command Centre]] (once the Command Centre has been built).

While participating in player-owned ports is members only, free-to-play players can enter the port via the portal in [[Port Sarim]]. [[Meg]], [[The Partner]], [[Seasinger Umi]], and [[port staff]] are present, but attempting to interact with any NPC in the area will prompt a message stating "You must be a member to use this feature".

==Getting there==
* The [[port portal]] to access the player-owned port can be found between [[Brian's Battleaxe Bazaar]] and [[the Rusty Anchor]], in the northern part of [[Port Sarim]]
* Another port portal is set on the southern side of the [[Menaphos Port district]]
* The [[Port portal (Prifddinas)|port portal in Prifddinas]] can be access from the [[Tower of Voices]]
* After completing the [[#Tutorial|tutorial]], the [[Captain's Log]] teleports players to the port

