===Time required===
In order to determine the (approximate) time the voyage will take the effective speed first needs to be calculated. The effective speed can be taken based on the maximum speed, the minimum speed and the ship's speed. The speed of the voyage is the average speed of the minimum effective speed and maximum effective speed of the voyage.

<math>
\begin{array}{lcl}
\text{speed}_{\text{max}} & = & \lfloor 1.25 \times \text{speed}_{\text{voyage}} \rfloor \\
\text{speed}_{\text{min}} & = & \lfloor 0.75 \times \text{speed}_{\text{voyage}} \rfloor \\
\text{speed}_{\text{effective}} & = & \text{max}(\text{min}(\text{speed}_{\text{max}},\text{speed}_{\text{ship}}),\text{speed}_{\text{min}}) \\
\end{array}
</math>

With the effective speed known it becomes possible to calculate the time in minutes using the following formula:

<math>
\text{time}_{\text{minutes}} = \text{max}\left (15, \left \lfloor \frac{1}{10} \times \left \lfloor \frac{\text{speed}_{\text{voyage}} \times \text{distance}}{\text{speed}_{\text{effective}}}\right \rfloor \right \rfloor \right )
</math>

This formula will give the exact time displayed in the game client. The actual times in-game might vary slightly. Also this means that the minimum time for a voyage will be 15 minutes, regardless of region, voyage or stats, with the exception of the tutorial mission.

In addition to this formula, activating the [[Totem of Navigation]] on Anachronia will provide a 15% reduction in the voyage time, although this still cannot reduce the time below the 15 minute minimum.

===Difficulty===
The difficulty level displayed on the interface is calculated based on the average of morale, combat, and seafaring statistics of the voyage. This is just a rough estimate for players and will not affect the actual voyage.

<math>
\begin{array}{lcl}
\overline{a}_{\text{v}} & = & (\text{morale}_{\text{voyage}} + \text{combat}_{\text{voyage}} + \text{seafaring}_{\text{voyage}}) \div 3 \\
\overline{d} & = & ((\text{morale}_{\text{voyage}} - \text{morale}_{\text{player}}) + (\text{combat}_{\text{voyage}} - \text{combat}_{\text{player}}) + (\text{seafaring}_{\text{voyage}} - \text{seafaring}_{\text{player}})) \div 3 \\

\text{difficulty} & = & 
\begin{cases}
0, & \text{if}\ \overline{a}_{\text{v}} = 0 \\
5, & \text{if}\ \overline{d} > \overline{a}_{\text{v}} \times \frac{3}{4} \\
4, & \text{if}\ \overline{d} > \overline{a}_{\text{v}} \times \frac{1}{4} \\
3, & \text{if}\ \overline{d} > 0 - \overline{a}_{\text{v}} \times \frac{1}{4} \\
2, & \text{if}\ \overline{d} > 0 - \overline{a}_{\text{v}} \times \frac{3}{4} \\
1, & \text{if}\ \overline{d} > \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
\end{array}
</math>

===Port updates===
{{Main|Player-owned port/Ports updates}}
Whilst on a voyage, the player may occasionally receive random updates about their ship. These do not impact on their ship's voyage in any way. These include random observations, notices, etc., which are mostly humorous.

==Regions==
[[File:Wushanko Isles map detail.png|thumb|center|600px|link=Map:Wushanko Isles|A map of the Wushanko Isles]]
Players begin with only [[the Arc]] unlocked. Progress toward unlocking additional regions ([[the Skull]], [[the Hook]], [[the Scythe]], [[the Bowl]], [[the Pincers]], [[the Loop]], and [[the Shield]]) is made as their ships undertake voyages, logging more distance travelled. Distance is travelled and progress is made regardless of the success or failure of a voyage. The [[Captain's Log]], given by Duncan [[the Navigator]], shows the player's total distance travelled on the Port statistics page.

Each region unlocked is progressively farther away than the last. For example, to unlock the Skull region, a distance of 5,000 must be travelled; however, to unlock the Hook region, a distance of 40,000 must be travelled. As each additional region unlocked is farther from the port, their voyages take longer and add greater distance; they also have higher adversity and give better rewards for success. Unlocking a region also unlocks new crew members from that region, with better base stats to help overcome the higher adversity.

